{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790730338,"nonce":"nu5aat2xlFsTiigwPzYGRmkmlVI=","title":"Native Bytes hex methods are missing from tiered conformance","message":"Issue8212 failed before its assertions with E0100, \"Cannot access field 'ofHex': class not registered or field does not exist\". `haxe.io.Bytes` aliases `rayzor.Bytes` for this target, and that extern declared neither `ofHex` nor `toHex` even though upstream Bytes exposes both.\n\nAdd the extern declarations, MIR runtime mappings, plugin symbols, and native UTF-8-hex conversion. The decoder follows the standard Haxe nibble conversion and throws on odd-length input; the encoder emits lowercase hex. A static method whose imported extern stub has no function ID must still use its native mapping. The missing-stub fallback is limited to methods declared on `rayzor.Bytes`: a broad fallback redirected Reflect.deleteField/hasField through raw native signatures and crashed Issue5016 and Issue5572 in the pilot run.\n\nVerification: Issue8212 now passes both assertions. BytesHex.hx covers uppercase input, lowercase output, and odd-length rejection. The full tiered corpus moved from 780/1094 to 781/1094, with Issue8212 the only status change. All 93 authored regressions pass. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` passes.","files":null}]}